<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_event_entertainment" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Stage Manager</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html">
            <p>Keeping a performer roster, setting up stages, building a Run of
            Show, and printing the sheet you'll hold during the show.</p>
        </field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('nonprofit_event_entertainment.group_entertainment_user')])]" />
    </record>

    <record id="section_roster" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">The performer roster</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_performers" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Adding performers</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>The roster lives under <strong>Events › Configuration › Performers</strong>, not on any one event. Add an act once, and it's ready for every event it plays.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Contact</strong> links to the person or group you deal with. It's optional.</li>
                    <li><strong>Genre</strong> and <strong>Default Set Length</strong> save typing later. The length fills in when you book the act.</li>
                    <li><strong>Technical Rider</strong> holds what they need: power, mics, monitors, backline.</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <img src="/nonprofit_elearning_event_entertainment/static/img/performer_form.png" alt="A performer form with contact, genre, default set length and tabs for the technical rider, notes and bookings" class="img-fluid" />
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>
                        a performer on the roster.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-history" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Their history comes with them</span>
                        <p>The <strong>Bookings</strong> tab shows every event an act has been booked for.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="section_stages" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Stages</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_stages" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Setting up stages</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>Open the event and go to its <strong>Entertainment</strong> tab. Add a line for each stage, such as Main Stage or Acoustic Tent, with its <strong>Start Time</strong>. Each stage runs its own schedule, independent of the others.</p>
                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <img src="/nonprofit_elearning_event_entertainment/static/img/event_entertainment.png" alt="An event's Entertainment tab with a count of stages and a list showing Main Stage" class="img-fluid" />
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>
                        the Entertainment tab on a sample event.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-map-marker" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Putting a stage on the map</span>
                        <p>If the event uses the Vendor Map, <strong>Place Stages</strong> on the map lets you click where a stage stands. You can also type its coordinates on the stage's form.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="section_show" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Building the show</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_run_of_show" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">The Run of Show</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">31</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>Open a stage to build its <strong>Run of Show</strong>. Each line is one of two kinds:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Performance</strong>: choose a performer. Their default set length fills in, and you can change it for this booking.</li>
                    <li><strong>Announcement</strong>: a title and a duration, for a raffle drawing, sponsor thank-yous, or a set change.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Drag lines into order. You don't type start times: each one follows from the stage's start time and the lengths before it, and they all update when you reorder.</p>
                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <img src="/nonprofit_elearning_event_entertainment/static/img/stage_form.png" alt="A stage's Run of Show with two performances and an announcement, with computed start times and booking status" class="img-fluid" />
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>
                        a Run of Show with times worked out.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_hard_time" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Hard times and booking status</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">32</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>Some things must happen at a set time, such as a headliner at 9:00 PM sharp. Enter that time under <strong>Hard Time</strong> on the line. It stays put, and everything after it follows from when it ends.</p>
                <p><strong>Booking State</strong> shows where each act stands: Invited, Confirmed, Declined, or Cancelled. Change it with the buttons at the end of the act's line: <strong>Confirm</strong>, <strong>Decline</strong>, or <strong>Cancel</strong>. If plans change again, or you clicked the wrong one, <strong>Re-invite</strong> puts the act back to Invited.</p>
                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">A declined act keeps its time slot</span>
                        <p>Declined and cancelled acts stay on the schedule and on the printed Run of Show, and later acts don't move up. To close the gap, delete the line or replace it with another act.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-exclamation-triangle" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">A hard time doesn't move earlier acts</span>
                        <p>Lines before it keep their calculated times, so check for a gap or an overlap just before a hard time.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="section_day" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">On the day</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">40</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_print" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Printing the Run of Show</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">41</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>Click <strong>Print Run of Show</strong> on the stage. You get one large-type sheet for that stage, showing clock time, item, and duration, with announcements marked differently from performances.</p>
                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-print" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Print late, and print each stage</span>
                        <p>Each stage has its own sheet. Print after your last change, because a reordered line changes every time below it.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="section_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">50</field>
    </record>

    <record id="slide_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_entertainment" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="slide_category">quiz</field>
        <field name="sequence">51</field>
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q1" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="question">You drag a performance earlier in the Run of Show. What happens to the times?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">You retype each start time</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">Times update automatically from the new order</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Nothing, until you print</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">The stage's start time changes</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="question">The headliner must start at 9:00 PM exactly. What do you do?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Set a Hard Time on that line</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">Add a separate stage</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Change the stage's start time to 9:00 PM</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Lengthen every act before it</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="question">Where do you add a raffle drawing to the schedule?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">On the performer roster</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">As an Announcement line in the Run of Show</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">In the event's Notes</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">It can't be scheduled</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="question">A band plays your festival every year. Where do you keep its technical needs?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Retype them on each event</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">In the event's description</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">On its performer record, under Technical Rider</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">On the printed sheet</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

</odoo>
